Z||000008||Fformula88||10-17-2001||05:43 PM||||Thats a surprise they wouldn't do exhaust work!!  The Fiero is a good car to rip someone off on in that department.  Since the Exhaust is held on almost exclusively by springs, it isn't a really big job to take down or put up.  I've seen guys cursing at those metal flanges on my Probe for over an hour while they burn the bolts off and have to drill out the holes to ra-attach everything!||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||10-17-2001||05:50 PM||||Ahh, what numbnuts! The guy you talked to must have been a product of Midas. I dropped and rehung a Fiero exhaust in a driveway in about 40 minutes. TOO easy. Plus, the exhaust isn't even half the length of a front engined cars exhaust. His loss. Keep looking around, you'll find a shop that will hang a Flowmaster in there!<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">     <BR>My Fiero website-&gt; <A HREF="http://www.dancinghamsters.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dancinghamsters.com/</A>||||reg||13
Z||000010||GTFiero1||10-17-2001||05:54 PM||||you should have asked them if they'd do work on a chevette <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Nashco||10-17-2001||10:41 PM||||Yeah, some shops can be soo retarded.  I once worked at a shop that had a policy when I started that they didn't work on air cooled VWs.  When I heard that I was like, "What the hell are you talking about????"  I own a 69 bug, and have unbolted every single thing on the car at least once...they by far the most simple car I have ever seen, let alone worked on.  So I convinced them to take one in once, and after seeing how much easier to deal with they were than standard cars they dropped their retarded policy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have had a couple people give me the, "Oh, it's a fiero?  That's probably going to cost more then," about doing an alignment.  Even after calming their fears of a complex system designed by nuclear physicists by telling them the only adjustments the car had, they still wouldn't believe me...silly folks I tell ya.  You'll get this; people seem to think "different from the ordinary" means "more complex and harder to work with" in many cases.<P>What I'm trying to get to is this: if they didn't work on your car just because of what it is, you didn't want them working on it anyway.  Anybody with a good mechanical knowledge and with a good business and customer service sense has no qualms with working on any kind of car.  My dad was this way, and I've learned well because of it.  Anything from changing the oil on an Escort to doing a 350 swap into a 914...he did it without any problems.  I'm the same way; some cars may be a little harder to work on, but if you know what you're doing, a good mechanic won't be afraid of anything.<P>This is one reason I ask the Fiero community for recommendations before getting any work I can't do, like exhuast (currently working on getting mine done too).  If somebody else had their's done and was pleased, chances are that I can trust that source.  Good luck with your ventures...and don't let those guys bother you, just laugh and walk away; they don't know what they're missing out on <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||grinthock||10-18-2001||09:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>That really sux...i wonder why they were like it, they aren't THAT hard to work on, especially for a pro shop.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually BlackStang they are not hard to work on at all.  I have worked on a couple mustangs, some of the older ones were not too bad, probably a little harder than the fiero though.  The new ones are ALOT more of a pain.<P>I saw one fiero once where I guy chopped a HOLE in the firewall to change the rear plugs.  And I sit and ask myself.  WHY!?  It's easier to change those plugs than changing them in most horizontal mounted V6/v8 cars!<P>Just my 2c.  BlackStang when are you getting your Fiero?||||reg||1
